  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Wet weather returns Friday night and Saturday.\n\nDry quiet weather again expected today across the entire Lower \nLakes. It may be a bit cooler across parts of the area in large part \ndue to a weak (dry) back door cold front dropping in across the \nregion. It will be this front that will then sets the stage for \nactive weather to return starting Friday with some showers.  \n\nA shortwave and a weak surface low tracking along this frontal \nboundary will bring a better chance for rain and showers Friday \nnight and Saturday. Blended guidance continuing to suggest the \ngreatest coverage will be across western New York, especially areas \nsouth of the NYS Thruway. At this point, rainfall amounts look to be \n0.50-0.75 south of Lake Ontario, tapering to a tenth of an inch or \nless across the North Country.\n\nDry weather returns Sunday behind the departing frontal wave with \nseasonable temperatures.",
